Subject: [BioC] scan date information
In-Reply-To: <4AB77B01.2070102@vt.edu>
References: <h972so$k1i$1@ger.gmane.org> <4AB77B01.2070102@vt.edu>
Message-ID: <4AB7A6BD.80609@fhcrc.org>

Robert,
The answer depends on which version of R and BioC are you using. If you 
are using R <= 2.9, BioC <= 2.4, you will need to devise your own 
method; one of which was given by Saroj. If you are using R-devel and 
BioC 2.5 (devel), the eSet abstract class and its derived classes such 
as ExpressionSet contain a new slot called protocolData that contains an 
AnnotatedDataFrame object. This slot is to be populated by metadata 
contained in microarray data files. In BioC 2.5 (devel) the 
read.affybatch from affy and read.celfile from affyio add a ScanData 
column to the protocolData slot with the metadata you are looking for.


Cheers,
Patrick


