 annotation "hugene10stv1cdf" to work with affylmGUI?!
Message-ID: <4ABA259D.4040203@unito.it>

Dear Olivia,
if you wish to analyze gene arrays using a graphical interface you can also use oneChannelGUI (http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.4/bioc/html/oneChannelGUI.html), which extends the functionalities of affylmGUI and uses apt tools, from Affymetrix, to intensity calculations, so you do not need cdf. Affy  libraries and gene data annotation are derived from Affymetrix and embedded internally.
Feel free to contact me if you need extra info on oneChannelGUI installation and usage.
Cheers
Raffaele

